// Model B — the CORRECT design: constrain the expressible, free the inexpressible.
// The freedom valve routes an inexpressible requirement to human judgment so it
// is "addressed" without being "formalized" — the gate no longer deadlocks.
DOMAIN gate

NOT req vrf_expressible

// freedom valve: what VRF can't express is deferred to human judgment, WITH a
// recorded rationale (deferred_to_freedom), not forced into VRF
RULE freedom_valve:
    WHEN NOT req vrf_expressible
    THEN req deferred_to_freedom

// a requirement is "addressed" either by being formalized OR deferred to freedom
RULE addressed_via_freedom:
    WHEN req deferred_to_freedom
    THEN req addressed
RULE addressed_via_formal:
    WHEN req formalized
    THEN req addressed

// verify needs every requirement ADDRESSED — not necessarily formalized
PREMISE verify_needs_addressed:
    WHEN spec verified
    THEN req addressed

PREMISE planning_needs_verify:
    WHEN plan entered
    THEN spec verified

FACT spec verified
FACT plan entered
CHECK
